                        "text": "<p><strong>Care Instructions for Your Plated or full gold Jewelry</strong><br/><br/>Our pieces are crafted to make a statement—and to stay with you for years. To keep their shine and spirit alive, a little mindful care goes a long way.<br/><br/>Here’s how to love them back:<br/><br/><strong>Last on, first off.</strong><br/>Put your jewelry on after applying perfume, lotion, or makeup—and take it off before undressing, showering, or sleeping.<br/><br/><strong>Keep it dry.</strong><br/>Water, humidity, and plating don’t mix. Avoid wearing your piece while swimming, bathing, or sweating.<br/><br/><strong>Soft touch only.</strong><br/>Clean gently with a soft, dry cloth after each wear to remove any natural oils or residue. No chemicals, no abrasives—just a little love.<br/><br/><strong>Store with intention.</strong><br/>Keep your piece in its Noritamy pouch or box, away from sunlight and other jewelry to prevent scratching or fading.<br/><br/><strong>Time to replate?</strong><br/>Over time, gold plating may naturally fade depending on wear. When that moment comes, we offer a re-plating service to bring your piece back to life.<br/><br/><strong>Materials: </strong></p>{{ closest.product.metafields.custom.materials | metafield_tag }}",
                        "width": "100%",
                        "max_width": "normal",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "type_preset": "rte",
                        "font": "var(--font-primary--family)",
